  "query_preview": "..\nDry conditions continue across the Marianas as the seasonal doldrums\nremain over the region. A few isolated showers are seen east of Guam,\nbut these have struggled to make it on land with little to no\nrainfall seen across the island today. A trade-wind surge will move\ninto the region this weekend bringing moderate to fresh winds. As the\ntrades build, showers may increase in coverage when trade-wind\nconvergence occurs. As of now the forecast keeps isolated showers in\nthe extended range, but there will be some potential for short \nperiods of scattered showers next week.",
